    schemeCitation: "Marking points quoted from the SEC marking scheme, History 2019 Higher Level — © State Examinations Commission.",
    id: "hist-2019-hl-em-s1-q3a", topicId: "hist-em-irl-1", conceptId: "light-think-plan-sensible",
    section: "1", questionRef: "2019 HL Early Modern Section 1 Q3(a)",
    stem: "Case study: The Plantation of Laois/Offaly",
    questionText: "In the light of both documents, do you think that the plan in document B is a sensible one? Explain your answer, referring to both documents.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "The plan in Doc. B is to change the type of lease offered to encourage more settlers into the area and for those settlers to pay the costs of their own defence", marks: null },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "It is also hoped to reduce the size of the army", marks: null },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "This is a sensible plan because the area is “virtually uninhabited” (Doc. A) and needs more settlers", marks: null },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "A change from copyhold to freehold leases, as outlined in Doc. B, would help attract more settlers", marks: null },
    { id: "r-5", kind: "point", verbatim: "Freehold leaseholders would be more likely to make the “costly investment necessary” (Doc. A) to defend the settlement", marks: null },
    { id: "r-6", kind: "point", verbatim: "The Privy Council has agreed to the change in leases, “especially for those who build forts and defences at their own expense” (Doc. B), which confirms that this is seen as a sensible plan", marks: null },
    { id: "r-7", kind: "point", verbatim: "The Privy Council also want to take advantage of “peace at home” (Doc. B) to reduce the size of the army, which costs 7,000 marks per year (Doc. A)", marks: null },
    { id: "r-8", kind: "point", verbatim: "It welcomes the opportunity to cut army numbers by licensing soldiers to serve abroad", marks: null },
    { id: "r-9", kind: "point", verbatim: "However, some candidates may argue that allowing soldiers to leave Ireland will endanger the security of the plantation and is therefore not sensible.", marks: null },
    ],
