    id: "hist-2022-hl-em-s1-q3a", topicId: "hist-em-irl-2", conceptId: "there-evidence-bias-reasons",
    section: "1", questionRef: "2022 HL Early Modern Section 1 Q3(a)",
    stem: "Case study: The clerical career of Meiler Magrath",
    questionText: "Is there evidence of bias in document A? Give reasons for your answer, referring to the document.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Yes and/or no. Evaluate the answer on the quality of the reasons given. The", marks: null },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "The writer is biased against Magrath. All the points made about him portray him in a negative light. No redeeming points are mentioned.", marks: null },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "The tone of the extract shows the writer’s bias. He expresses shock (“a mere layman”) or sympathy (the “poor man’s head”) to emphasise the depths of Magrath’s depravity.", marks: null },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "He reminds the reader that Magrath is “forgetting the honour due to his position as Archbishop” to make his behaviour sound more scandalous.", marks: null },
    { id: "r-5", kind: "point", verbatim: "He adds in his own negative opinions rather than confining himself to facts. He mentions the train of “armed men” and adds that this causes “great terror” and is a “bad example” to the people. This may not be true.", marks: null },
    { id: "r-6", kind: "point", verbatim: "He probably exaggerates the description of John O’Mullony’s injuries.", marks: null },
    { id: "r-7", kind: "point", verbatim: "It might be argued that the writer is not biased as he supports his allegations against Magrath with the names of people and places (Tadhg O’Hiffernan, Cahirconlish, etc). The writer is giving a factual account of Magrath’s bad behaviour.", marks: null },
    { id: "r-8", kind: "point", verbatim: "The allegations made are based on facts rather than bias, and this is proved by Magrath’s defence in doc B, where he does not deny that any of these incidents took place.", marks: null },
    ],
