    stem: "Case study: The Plantation of Laois‐Offaly",
    questionText: "In what ways is document B a useful source for the historian investigating the Plantation of Laois‐Offaly? Make reference to the document in your answer.",
    tariffModel: {"kind":"questionTotal"}, totalMarks: 10,
    rows: [
    { id: "r-1", kind: "point", verbatim: "Doc B is a useful historical source on the Laois Offaly Plantation.", marks: null, contextNote: "Comments on the limitations of the document should also be accepted. — Points should be supported by reference to doc B.", openList: true },
    { id: "r-2", kind: "point", verbatim: "The account was written in 1558, and is a primary source of evidence on the background to the Plantation.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-3", kind: "point", verbatim: "The writer is supportive of British rule in Ireland and gives a very hostile account of the “wild Irish”. Although it is a biased account, this document provides evidence of how the English viewed the “barbarous” Irish.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-4", kind: "point", verbatim: "The document provides evidence of a sense of crisis for English rule in Ireland at the time. English power is threatened with “extinction”, the small army and lack of funds mean that war against the Irish is “futile”. A settlement must be reached “at any cost”.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-5", kind: "point", verbatim: "The document shows English policy in Ireland was determined by expedience rather that by “what is right”.", marks: null, openList: true },
    { id: "r-6", kind: "point", verbatim: "Factual details such as the size of the English army in Ireland and the potential rental income from the lands of Laois and Offaly are useful information for historians, etc.", marks: null, openList: true },
    ],
